/*  FIT A BINARY PAIR TO MEASURED DATA, THEN TEST IT ON DATA IT NEVER SAW.

    `fitParameters` regresses two NRTL coefficients (b_ij, b_ji) of the
    ethanol-water pair, starting from zero (Raoult's law), on TEN measured
    bubble points at 101.3 kPa, then predicts FOUR further measured points
    frozen out of the fit before anything was run (every third point).  The
    band the held-out error must meet was declared before the fit.

    What to read in the output, in order:
      * the T-x-y diagram -- Raoult, the fitted NRTL, the fit and held-out
                             points drawn as separate series;
      * HELD-OUT EVIDENCE -- the average absolute deviation on the four
                             points the fit never saw, and the verdict;
      * identifiability   -- with two parameters on one isobar the fit is
                             well posed (the run reports the condition number).

    The run writes `ethanol-water.proposal.dat`, the fitted pair with its
    evidence, its verdict and its band, plus the fit log and the parity table.
    The full design is in system/propsDict. */
tier          tutorial;
application   choupoProps;
description     "Fit an ethanol-water NRTL pair (two parameters, starting from Raoult) to ten measured bubble points at 101.3 kPa, test it on four held-out points, draw the T-x-y diagram";
verbosity     3;
